 recipients supported through end-2023","published_date":null,"source_type":"third_party_report"}],"investors":[],"note_en":"Official EIF final-recipient list explicitly names E-Flight Academy B.V., de Zanden 167, 7395 PG Teuge, as a Loan / Guarantee recipient; name and address match the academy. List covers support through end-2023, which is a coverage cutoff, not an announcement or signing date. Individual amount, lender, guarantee size, loan terms, dates and cash received are not disclosed. EIF is not inferred to be the direct lender. This is a support disclosure, not an additive funding total; overlap with other loan disclosures is unestablished.","coverage_note_en":"Partial public-source review through 2026-11-15. Exact issuer, contract/debt/grant boundaries and publication dates checked; unknown private funding and unretrieved earlier history remain unknown."},{"company_slug":"eclecticiq","round_key":"eclecticiq-2025-06-30-cti-ai-digital-europe-grant","stage":"CTI-AI Digital Europe grant disclosure","financing_type":"grant","announced_date":"2025-06-30","amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":"undisclosed","closing_status":"announced","record_kind":"investment_disclosure","amount_qualifier":"exact","research_status":"partial","checked_at":"2026-11-15","publication_status":"approved","sources":[{"url":"https://www.eclecticiq.com/projects/cti-ai","title":"CTI-AI — Digital Europe project","published_date":"2025-06-30","source_type":"company_announcement"},{"url":"https://www.eclecticiq.com/news/european-consortium-awarded-digital-europe-program-grant-to-enhance-ai-driven-cyber-threat-intelligence-capabilities","title":"European Consortium Awarded Digital Europe Program Grant to Enhance AI-Driven Cyber Threat Intelligence Capabilities","published_date":"2025-07-10","source_type":"company_announcement"}],"investors":[{"slug":"european-union","name":"European Union","entity_type":"Government agency","role":"grantor","source_index":0,"id":"b1c6839d-4f1e-42ea-9632-328bec498312"}],"note_en":"Company project page identifies CTI-AI under Digital Europe grant agreement 101190156 and lists EclecticIQ eligible project costs EUR1,876,449.37 with a 50% grant rate. Eligible project cost is not grant proceeds. The implied half-cent calculation does not establish a published exact company grant allocation, so amount remains undisclosed. Consortium total funding/budget is not attributed to this company. Earliest retrieved company project publication is 2025-06-30, preceding the 2025-07-10 news release; no assertion of payment or exact signing date.","coverage_note_en":"Partial public-source review through 2026-11-15. Exact issuer, contract/debt/grant boundaries and publication dates checked; unknown private funding and unretrieved earlier history remain unknown."},{"company_slug":"edgecortix","round_key":"diu-resource-optimized-compute-ot-2025","stage":"DIU prototype OT contract","financing_type":"undisclosed","record_kind":"investment_disclosure","announced_date":"2025-05-12","amount":null,"currency":null,"amount_basis":"undisclosed","closing_status":"announced","amount_qualifier":"exact","research_status":"partial","publication_status":"approved","checked_at":"2026-11-15","note_en":"EdgeCortix announced a DIU Other Transaction prototype award to the Japanese company and its U.S.-based subsidiary, secured in February 2025. The release and DIU identify EdgeCortix; the contract amount and allocation between legal recipients are undisclosed. This is a joint R&D contract disclosure, not an equity round or a claim of parent-only cash proceeds. May 12 is the public announcement date, not February award timing.","coverage_note_en":"Partial original-source review through 2026-11-15. Contract values and agency roles are distinct from equity proceeds; complete financing history remains unresolved.","sources":[{"url":"https://www.edgecortix.com/en/press-releases/edgecortix-becomes-first-japanese-and-semiconductor-company-awarded-u.s.-defense-innovation-unit-contract","title":"EdgeCortix becomes first Japanese and semiconductor company awarded U.S. Defense Innovation Unit contract","published_date":"2025-05-12","disposition":"Primary original opened and reviewed","source_type":"company_announcement"},{"url":"https://www.diu.mil/latest/hybrid-space-communications-network-leverages-commercial-technology-enabling","title":"DIU: Hybrid Space Communications Network Leverages Commercial Technology","published_date":"2025-05-12","disposition":"Primary original opened and reviewed","source_type":"investor_announcement"}],"investors":[{"slug":"us-defense-innovation-unit","name":"U.S. Defense Innovation Unit","entity_type":"Government agency","role":"undisclosed","source_index":0}]},{"company_slug":"electra","round_key":"afrl-ico-hybrid-electric-testing-2026","stage":"AFRL ICO R&D contract","financing_type":"undisclosed","record_kind":"investment_disclosure","announced_date":"2026-11-09","amount":4700000,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"announced_round_size","closing_status":"announced","amount_qualifier":"exact","research_status":"partial","publication_status":"approved","checked_at":"2026-11-15","note_en":"Electra announced a $4.7 million U.S. Air Force Research Laboratory Innovative Capabilities Opening R&D contract for hybrid-electric ground and flight testing. Recipient Electra Defense is explicitly Electra’s business unit in its December 2025 launch release. The figure is announced contract value, not equity, a grant or demonstrated cash received. The Air Force is the contracting party; participant role remains undisclosed under the available financing-role taxonomy.","coverage_note_en":"Partial original-source review through 2026-11-15. Contract values and agency roles are distinct from equity proceeds; complete financing history remains unresolved.","sources":[{"url":"https://electra.aero/news/us-air-force-awards-electra-defense-47-million-rd-contract-for-hybrid-electric-aircraft-testing","title":"U.S. Air Force awards Electra Defense $4.7 million R&D contract for hybrid-electric aircraft testing","published_date":"2026-11-09","disposition":"Primary original opened and reviewed","source_type":"company_announcement"},{"url":"https://electra.aero/news/electra-launches-defense-unit","title":"Electra launches defense business unit","published_date":"2025-12-03","disposition":"Primary original opened and reviewed","source_type":"company_announcement"}],"investors":[{"slug":"us-air-force","name":"US Air Force","entity_type":"Government agency","role":"undisclosed","source_index":0,"id":"9cd5444a-bb10-4e76-a381-d5ac7ffeb195"}]}],"relationships":[{"company_slug":"dronery","investor":{"slug":"cando-drones","name":"Cando Drones Ltd.","entity_type":"corporate"},"source":{"url":"https://www.droneryfly.com/about-us/","title":"Dronery About Us: subsidiary of Cando Drones LTD","source_type":"company_announcement","published_date":null},"note_en":"Dronery identifies itself as a subsidiary of Cando Drones LTD. This supports parent ownership only, without a disclosed investment date, amount or ownership percentage. Cando parent IPO or other parent financing is not attributed to the subsidiary."},{"company_slug":"e-flight-academy","investor":{"slug":"transavia-ventures","name":"Transavia Ventures B.V.","entity_type":"Corporate venture capital"},"source":{"url":"https://news.transavia.com/en/transavia-student-pilots-fly-electrically-for-the-first-time/","title":"Transavia student pilots fly electrically for the first time","published_date":"2025-03-18","source_type":"investor_announcement"},"note_en":"Transavia corporate announcement explicitly says E-Flight Academy is one of the initiatives in which Transavia Ventures invests. Generic investment relationship only: original round date, security, amount, participant role and individual contribution are not disclosed. Pilot training cooperation is not itself treated as financing."}]}'::jsonb; matched integer; begin
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.investor_research(research_id,slug,name,entity_type,evidence_status,evidence_status_label,evidence_basis,source_dataset,source_dataset_version,publication_status,map_ready,verified_as_of,approved_at,missing_fields) select distinct 'funding-research:'||(p->>'slug'),p->>'slug',p->>'name',p->>'entity_type','deal','Source-confirmed financing participant','primary_or_transaction_party',(select data->>'dataset' from input),(select data->>'checked_at' from input),'approved',false,(r->>'checked_at')::date,now(),array['Published offices','Fund size / manager AUM','Typical ticket size','Investment mandate'] from participants on conflict(slug) do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.investor_research(research_id,slug,name,entity_type,evidence_status,evidence_status_label,evidence_basis,source_dataset,source_dataset_version,publication_status,map_ready,verified_as_of,approved_at,missing_fields) select 'funding-research:'||(g->'investor'->>'slug'),g->'investor'->>'slug',g->'investor'->>'name',g->'investor'->>'entity_type','deal','Company-confirmed investor listing','company_published_investors',(select data->>'dataset' from input),(select data->>'checked_at' from input),'approved',false,(select(data->>'checked_at')::date from input),now(),array['Published offices','Round attribution','Individual contribution'] from generic on conflict(slug) do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.company_funding_rounds(company_id,round_key,stage,financing_type,announced_date,amount,currency,amount_basis,closing_status,note_en,publication_status,checked_at,record_kind,parent_round_id,amount_qualifier) select c.id,r->>'round_key',r->>'stage',r->>'financing_type',r->>'announced_date',(r->>'amount')::numeric,r->>'currency',r->>'amount_basis',r->>'closing_status',r->>'note_en','approved',(r->>'checked_at')::date,coalesce(r->>'record_kind','round'),null::uuid,coalesce(r->>'amount_qualifier','exact') from rounds join public.companies c on c.slug::text=r->>'company_slug'  where coalesce(r->>'record_kind','round')<>'extension' on conflict(company_id,round_key) do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.company_funding_rounds(company_id,round_key,stage,financing_type,announced_date,amount,currency,amount_basis,closing_status,note_en,publication_status,checked_at,record_kind,parent_round_id,amount_qualifier) select c.id,r->>'round_key',r->>'stage',r->>'financing_type',r->>'announced_date',(r->>'amount')::numeric,r->>'currency',r->>'amount_basis',r->>'closing_status',r->>'note_en','approved',(r->>'checked_at')::date,coalesce(r->>'record_kind','round'),parent.id,coalesce(r->>'amount_qualifier','exact') from rounds join public.companies c on c.slug::text=r->>'company_slug' join public.company_funding_rounds parent on parent.company_id=c.id and parent.round_key=r->>'parent_round_key' where coalesce(r->>'record_kind','round')='extension' on conflict(company_id,round_key) do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.company_funding_round_sources(round_id,url,title,source_type,checked_at) select f.id,s->>'url',s->>'title',s->>'source_type',(r->>'checked_at')::date from rounds join public.companies c on c.slug::text=r->>'company_slug' join public.company_funding_rounds f on f.company_id=c.id and f.round_key=r->>'round_key' cross join lateral jsonb_array_elements(r->'sources') s on conflict(round_id,url) do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.company_funding_round_investors(round_id,investor_research_id,role,source_url,checked_at,contribution_amount,contribution_currency) select f.id,i.id,p->>'role',r->'sources'->((p->>'source_index')::int)->>'url',(r->>'checked_at')::date,(p->'contribution'->>'amount')::numeric,p->'contribution'->>'currency' from participants join public.companies c on c.slug::text=r->>'company_slug' join public.company_funding_rounds f on f.company_id=c.id and f.round_key=r->>'round_key' join public.investor_research i on i.slug::text=p->>'slug' on conflict(round_id,investor_research_id) do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.investor_research_sources(investor_id,url,title,accessed_at) select distinct i.id,r->'sources'->((p->>'source_index')::int)->>'url',r->'sources'->((p->>'source_index')::int)->>'title',(r->>'checked_at')::date from participants join public.investor_research i on i.slug::text=p->>'slug' where not exists(select 1 from public.investor_research_sources ex where ex.investor_id=i.id and ex.url=r->'sources'->((p->>'source_index')::int)->>'url' and ex.location_id is null) on conflict do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.investor_companies(investor_research_id,company_id,relationship_type,evidence_status,source_url,reviewed_at,portfolio_name_as_published,match_method,match_note_en) select i.id,c.id,'portfolio_listed','company_published_investors',g->'source'->>'url',(select(data->>'checked_at')::date from input),c.name,'manual',g->>'note_en' from generic join public.investor_research i on i.slug::text=g->'investor'->>'slug' join public.companies c on c.slug::text=g->>'company_slug' on conflict(investor_research_id,company_id,relationship_type) do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.investor_research_sources(investor_id,url,title,accessed_at) select distinct i.id,g->'source'->>'url',g->'source'->>'title',(select(data->>'checked_at')::date from input) from generic join public.investor_research i on i.slug::text=g->'investor'->>'slug' where not exists(select 1 from public.investor_research_sources ex where ex.investor_id=i.id and ex.url=g->'source'->>'url' and ex.location_id is null) on conflict do nothing;
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) insert into public.company_investment_research(company_id,coverage_status,coverage_note_en,checked_at,source_urls) select c.id,'partial',min(r->>'coverage_note_en'),max((r->>'checked_at')::date),array_agg(distinct s->>'url') from rounds join public.companies c on c.slug::text=r->>'company_slug' cross join lateral jsonb_array_elements(r->'sources') s group by c.id on conflict(company_id) do update set coverage_note_en=excluded.coverage_note_en,checked_at=excluded.checked_at,source_urls=(select array_agg(distinct u order by u) from unnest(company_investment_research.source_urls||excluded.source_urls) u),updated_at=now() where company_investment_research.coverage_status='partial' and (select data->>'dataset' from input)<>'company-funding-pilot-v1';
with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) select count(*) into matched from rounds join public.companies c on c.slug::text=r->>'company_slug' join public.company_funding_rounds f on f.company_id=c.id and f.round_key=r->>'round_key'; if matched<>15 then raise exception 'Manifest events did not all resolve';end if; if exists(with input as(select funding_payload as data), rounds as(select value r from input,jsonb_array_elements(data->'rounds')), participants as(select r,value p from rounds,jsonb_array_elements(r->'investors')), generic as(select value g from input,jsonb_array_elements(coalesce(data->'relationships','[]'::jsonb))) select 1 from rounds join public.companies c on c.slug::text=r->>'company_slug' join public.company_funding_rounds f on f.company_id=c.id and f.round_key=r->>'round_key' where row(f.stage,f.financing_type,f.announced_date,f.amount,f.currency::text,f.amount_basis,f.closing_status,f.record_kind,f.amount_qualifier) is distinct from row(r->>'stage',r->>'financing_type',r->>'announced_date',(r->>'amount')::numeric,r->>'currency',r->>'amount_basis',r->>'closing_status',coalesce(r->>'record_kind','round'),coalesce(r->>'amount_qualifier','exact'))) then raise exception 'Manifest conflicts with stored event: review instead of overwriting';end if;end $funding_import$;